{"id": "valpaca0098", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So pearls are formed when a foreign object enter s the oyster and the oyster covers it with nacre, which is what makes up the pearl. And they can be found in saltwater o ysters around the world, but they're not very common because only about 1% of oysters produce pearl s.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0102", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The largest star in our galaxy is UY Scuti. It's a red supergiant that has a radius about 1,7 00 times larger than the sun.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0106", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Sure, I can help with that. Do you know the formula for finding the area of a regular polygon?", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0110", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, I' ll tell you a story about some cats living in an apartment building. It's a tall building, and it has many floors. The cats are all different colors and shapes and sizes, but they all live together in the same building. They have their own rooms, of course, but they also share common spaces like hall ways and stairwells. Some of the cats are friendly with each other, while others are not so friendly. There's one cat named Whiskers who is very curious and likes to explore every nook and cranny of the building. Another cat named Mittens is more laid-back and prefers to lounge around in her favorite spot on the windowsill. But even though they may seem different from each other, they all have one thing in common: they're all immortal. That means that they can't die of old age or any other natural cause. Instead, they just keep living forever, going through countless lifetimes without ever aging. So what does this mean for them? Well, it means that they' ve seen a lot of things over the years. They' ve watched empires rise and fall, witnessed history' s greatest moments, and experienced everything from joy to sorrow.", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 60, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0114", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The wreath has been a symbol of Christmas since the Middle Ages. It' s thought that it may have originated in Germany, where people would hang them on their doors to ward off evil spirit s.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0118", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Yeah, they did.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 2, "carrier_ended": null}
