{"id": "valpaca0130", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, I mean, I think the most important thing is to be able to take a step back and look at things objectively rather than getting caught up in them. And also try to find ways to relax that work for you personally. For me, it's usually exercise or spending time with friends and family.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0134", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The most important difference is that plant-based proteins don' t contain any animal protein s. So if you're allergic to eggs or milk, for example, then you can eat these products without worrying about getting an allergic reaction from them.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0138", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "And so the first thing we' ve done is to create a culture of trust. So that people are comfortable speaking up when they have concerns, and then we listen to them. And I think that's really important because if you don't listen to people, then they're not going to speak up. And then once we've got those issues raised, we try and resolve them quickly. So we try and get things resolved as soon as possible so that it doesn't escalate into something bigger.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0142", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "And so I think that is something else that' s really interesting about language and culture. It's not just about the words themselves, but also how we use them in different contexts to convey meaning and build relationships with others. So it's a very complex topic. But if you want to learn more about it, there are some great books out there on this subject matter.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0146", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So I think the thing that's interesting about social media is, of course, we have this incredible opportunity to communicate with each other. But what' s also really interesting is how much news we get from it now. And so you see these algorithm s trying to find out what kind of content will keep us engaged and active on their platforms. And a lot of times that means sensational ized headlines or click baits or things like that. And then they'll just be sharing those over and over again without any context around them. So it can be hard to know if something's true or not. So one thing that I would recommend is when you see something that seems really surprising or shocking, try to look for more information about it before you share it with others.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 29, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0150", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "As a pirate captain, I would say to my crew, gather around and listen closely. There is a legend of hidden treasure buried on an un charted island, guarded by the sea itself. This gold, this silver, this precious j ewelry is not just wealth; it is our destiny. The wind whispers secrets to those who dare sail into the unknown. Together, we will brave the storm, navigate treacherous waters, and uncover riches beyond imagination. Our journey will be tough, but with courage in our hearts and determination in our sails, we will find that treasure. For every wave we conquer, for every challenge we overcome, we draw closer to our fortune. So hoist the colors, sharpen your blades, and set course for adventure!", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0154", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "With just a few seconds left on the clock, the game is tied. The crowd is on its feet as both teams are fighting for the win. The home team has possession of the ball and they're pushing forward. They get it into the hands of their star player, who makes a quick pass to the corner of the field. The receiver catch es it with ease and runs toward the goal line. There' s only one second left on the clock when he crosses into the end zone. T he crowd erupts in cheers as the team celebrate s their victory over their opponent. It was an incredible play that will be remembered by fans for years to come.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 26, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0158", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "I've been living in this wasteland for years, and every day is a struggle to survive. The air is thick with dust, and the only water comes from hidden spring s or rain that barely falls anymore. I travel alone most of the time, but occasionally, I come across other survivor s. There are those who have lost hope and just wander aimless ly, and then there are others like me, tough enough to endure. I' ve formed a loose alliance with a few people— a former mechanic who knows how to fix broken vehicles, a young girl who can still read old books, and an old nurse who tends to our injuries. We share what little we have, and sometimes, just sometimes, we find food or medicine. But trust is scarce out here; everyone looks out for themselves first. Still, when we help each other, it feels like a small victory in this broken world.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 39, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0162", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, there are a few things you can do. One is to ask questions that don' t have easy answers. If they're really interested in what you're saying, then they'll probably be able to answer them. But if not, then it's just small talk.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0166", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "But you can also tell a lot by looking at what other people are doing. So if you go to a place where they have some kind of tradition or ritual that' s going on, and you're just observing it as an outsider, but then you see somebody else who's participating in the same way, you know that there's something about this behavior that is important to them.And so even though you may not understand exactly why they're doing it, you can start to figure out which things are important to them based on how they act. And I think that's one of the most powerful ways to learn about culture is just by watching other people and seeing what they do.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 31, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0170", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A grain of salt is really small, so it's hard to count all the atoms in it. But we can figure out how many there are by using some basic science. First, a grain of salt is made up of tiny crystals called NaCl, which stands for sodium chloride. Each crystal has millions of sodium and chlorine atom s packed together in a regular pattern. Now, if we take a look at the size of a gra in of salt under a micro scope, it's about 0.1 mill imeters across, or roughly one-t housandth of an inch. That' s really tiny! Since each Na Cl molecule is super small, too, we need to use something called Avog adro's number to estimate how many molecules fit into that space. Avogadro' s number tells us that there are around 6. 0 22 times ten to the twenty-third particles in just one mo le of any substance. So, even though it sounds like a lot, when you break down the size of a gra in of salt, there are actually trillions upon trillions of atoms inside it.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 47, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0174", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "I would estimate that there are around 50 billion words spoken every day on Earth. This is based on the assumption that each person speak s approximately 1 5,000 words per day and there are about 3 3 billion people in the world. However, this number could be higher or lower depending on various factors such as language, culture, and communication habits.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0178", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "It's hard to say how many songs have been recorded throughout history because there are so many different types of music from all over the world, and new ones are being created every day. But we can look at some estimates based on historical data. For example, according to a report by the International Fo undation for Intellig ent Music Publishing, there are around 2 million songs in existence today. However, this number only includes recorded song s and does not account for traditional folk music or songs that were never officially recorded. If we consider ancient musical traditions and oral histories, the number could be much higher.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 27, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0182", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, I think he would have been a biologist. He was very interested in biology. In fact, his early work was actually on the properties of light. And then later he became more interested in physics and mathematics. But if he had focused on biology, he probably would have been a bi ologist.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0186", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, that's the thing. We don't know why they collapse d, but if we did, then maybe we could do something about it. But as far as I know, nobody knows why they collapsed.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0190", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Sure, I can help you with that. Here’s a sample resignation letter you can use as a guide. You might want to personalize it with your own details, but this should give you a good starting point. Dear [ Manager's Name], I hope this message finds you well. After careful consideration, I am writing to inform you of my decision to resign from my position at [Company Name]. My last day will be [last day of work], which gives me ample time to wrap up my responsibilities and ensure a smooth transition for the team. I have really enjoyed my time here and appreciate the opportunities I have had to grow and contribute. The support and mentorship from you and the entire team have been invaluable to me. This decision wasn ’t easy, but I believe it’ s the right step for my next career chapter. I am committed to supporting the hand off of my projects during my remaining time and making sure everything is in good hands. If there are any specific tasks or training needed before my departure, please let me know. Thank you again for the chance", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 60, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0194", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Jazz is a genre of music that originated in the southern United States during the late 19 th and early 2 0th centuries. It was born out of African- American communities, particularly in New Orleans, Louisiana, where it evolved from a blend of African rhythms and European musical traditions. The history of jazz is deeply tied to the social and cultural context of its time. During the Jim Crow era, when segregation was rampant, jazz provided a space for African-American artists to express themselves freely, often in places like speakeasies and ju deo l es, which were hidden venues for entertainment during Pro hib ition. Jazz became known for its improvisation, syncop ated rhythms, and unique instrument ation, including the saxophone, trumpet, piano, and double bass. Over time, jazz spread across the country and eventually around the world, influencing countless other genres such as rock, soul, and hip-hop. Some of the most iconic figures in jazz include Louis Armstrong, Duke Ellington, Miles Davis, and Ella Fitzgerald. Their contributions helped shape the sound and style of jazz as we know it today. Cult urally, jazz has played a significant role in advancing civil rights and challenging social norms. It symbolized freedom, creativity, and resistance, especially during times of racial tension. Jazz also fostered a sense of community and unity among diverse groups of people who came together to enjoy the music. Today , jazz continues to thrive, with new generation s of musicians pushing the boundaries of the genre while honor ing its rich heritage. Whether you're listening to a", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 60, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0198", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The orchestra's performance was absolutely stunning. The conductor led the ensemble with such passion and precision that it was impossible not to be swept up in the music. Each section of the orchestra played with remarkable skill, creating a rich tapestry of sound that filled the concert hall from start to finish. The audience was completely capt ivated, with many people sitting on the edge of their seats during the more intense moments. Overall, it was an unforgettable experience that left everyone in attendance feeling both exhilarated and deeply moved.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
